content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-113 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22650; high drive-end vibration reported after motor replacement.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration is 4.8 mm/s. The applicable manufacturer limit/classification is Figure 3 Zone C, 4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS on bearing housings: the reading is above the 4.5 mm/s Zone B/C boundary and below the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary, so it is 'Restricted - plan maintenance.' It is not presently in Zone D and therefore does not, by itself, trigger the SSP-07 immediate-stop rule. P2 planned maintenance is appropriate, subject to confirming the other housing reading and classifying the highest reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reported housing temperature is 70 C. Against the manufacturer's bearing-housing surface-temperature limits, this is exactly at the upper end of 'normal up to 70 C,' below the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip. It does not meet SSP-07's trigger for a priority-1 work order, which is temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported. The evidence supplies no numerical allowable-leakage limit; its troubleshooting action for replacing a mechanical seal applies to the symptom 'leakage at shaft seal.' The present report therefore does not establish a leakage-driven seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely first: shaft misalignment associated with the recent motor replacement. Misalignment is a documented cause of high vibration, and the manual specifically requires laser alignment after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear remains possible but is unconfirmed; it is a documented cause of high vibration. The 70 C housing reading alone does not demonstrate high bearing temperature because it is at, not above, the normal upper limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or impeller damage is another documented possible cause requiring inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation is a documented possible cause; the prescribed troubleshooting check is NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "During initial field checks, confirm that the reported 4.8 mm/s value is an RMS bearing-housing measurement. Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings, record the drive-end and non-drive-end values, and classify the highest value using Figure 3. Also record bearing-housing surface temperatures for comparison with the 70/80/90 C limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Obtain the motor-replacement and any post-replacement alignment records. Verify shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool, recording as-found and final values. Bring parallel offset within 0.05 mm and angular misalignment within 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Repeat alignment after any subsequent work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump or working on its seal, complete the electrical and mechanical isolation, drain/vent and line-break permit controls listed under safety_controls. Inspect the bearings and impeller for the documented high-vibration causes and check NPSH for cavitation. Do not condemn a component solely from the vibration reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If inspection shows that either bearing has wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair. If no such finding is made, bearing replacement is not authorised by the current evidence alone.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any disturbed joints covered by manual Table 5, reassemble using lightly oiled threads and the specified torques: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm; M24 impeller nut 160 Nm; M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm. Do not use Table 5's general 25 Nm seal-gland torque for seal work on this serial; the applicable bulletin value for an HF3-450B installation is 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to service, complete any required final laser alignment and restore the documented Plan 11 seal-flush arrangement from pump discharge; never run the pump dry. After restart, repeat vibration measurements on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading, and record the housing temperature. Apply the Zone D stop and temperature escalation controls below if triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "If the highest verified vibration reading falls in Figure 3 Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. Zone D is labelled 'Damage likely - stop the pump.' The current 4.8 mm/s reading is not in that zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, provide electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate both suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the back pull-out assembly is lifted, treat it as a 68 kg lift requiring lifting equipment. Because it exceeds 25 kg, use certified lifting equipment and a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If P-113 is confirmed to be on a chemically dosed line, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for the work. SSP-07 specifically identifies P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line as sodium-hypochlorite dosed, but does not establish P-113's service.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing temperature rises above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift. The documented manufacturer trip temperature is 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Base planned allowance for laser alignment: 1.5 hours with 1 technician for each alignment task. Additional alignment time will be needed if the task must be repeated after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional allowance only if inspection establishes the need for bearing replacement: replace the bearing pair in 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part and gland-torque conflict resolved for this asset: manual Table 5 lists M10 seal gland nuts at 25 Nm, while Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, requires 30 Nm with cartridge seal HF3-450B for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-113 is serial HF3-22650 and therefore falls within the bulletin range. For any seal work on this pump, do not fit HF3-450; use pre-set HF3-450B, with no sleeve measurement needed, and torque its gland nuts to 30 Nm rather than 25 Nm. Pumps below HF3-22000 remain on HF3-450 and manual Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The manual requires inspection of the seal sleeve for scoring but gives no numerical rejection threshold. The serial-applicable bulletin supplements this for P-113: replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. This is conditional on seal/sleeve work being added; no leakage-driven seal work is presently established.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Confirm that the reported 4.8 mm/s is RMS and was measured on the bearing housing, and obtain the non-drive-end reading. The manual requires measurement on both housings and classification of the highest reading; the single reported value may not establish the pump's final zone. (C06, C07)",
    "Confirm that the reported 70 C housing reading is a bearing-housing surface measurement and identify which housing was measured, because that is the measurement basis for the manual's temperature limits. (C01, C02)",
    "No as-found alignment values or contractor laser-alignment record are provided. Obtain any record, but retain the field verification task because the motor was replaced and no final alignment result is evidenced. (C10)",
    "Bearing condition, impeller condition and NPSH data are absent, so bearing wear, impeller imbalance/damage and cavitation cannot yet be confirmed or excluded. No NPSH acceptance value or test procedure is included in the evidence. (C09)",
    "Bearing and impeller part numbers are not supplied. Identify the correct parts before authorising replacements; if bearings are replaced, the manual requires both bearings as a pair. No inspection-only parts are presently justified. (C09, C10)",
    "P-113's chemical-dosing status is not stated. Confirm it before work so that the conditional chemical goggles and nitrile-glove control can be applied correctly; the only named chemically dosed pumps in the evidence are P-101 to P-106. (C15, C16)",
    "Figure 3 does not state which zone owns a value exactly on the 2.8, 4.5 or 7.1 mm/s boundaries. If a final reading falls exactly on a boundary, obtain reliability-engineering direction rather than inventing a boundary rule. (C07)",
    "The evidence gives no Zone C completion deadline and no standard labour times for diagnostic measurements, bearing/impeller inspection or the NPSH check. The planner must set the outage date and those labour allowances after scope is confirmed; only alignment and the listed replacement tasks have standard times. (C07, C09, C12)",
    "If seal work is subsequently added, confirm the required thread condition for SB-2026-014's 30 Nm gland torque: Table 5 specifies lightly oiled threads for its manual torques, but the bulletin does not state a thread-lubrication condition for its revised torque. (C11, C13)"
  ]
}
